BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8e5112208bb16325@resonance-log
DTSTAMP:20260905T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Revisit: Build vs Buy in the Age of AI
DESCRIPTION:AI build tools do not replace SaaS\, because business software 
 encodes hidden compliance and policy rules. The future is buy core SaaS\, 
 then layer AI agents and custom workflows on top\, with the PM uncovering 
 those rules and making the pieces work together.\n\nWhy it resonated: It r
 eframes build versus buy as an integration problem rather than a binary ch
 oice\, which is a more useful way to think about it.\n\nhttps://www.svpg.c
 om/article-build-vs-buy-in-the-age-of-ai/
URL:https://www.svpg.com/article-build-vs-buy-in-the-age-of-ai/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c214ca6ca65135f9@resonance-log
DTSTAMP:20260905T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261208
SUMMARY:Revisit: 10 Usability Heuristics for User Interface Design
DESCRIPTION:Ten durable rules of thumb for finding usability problems in an
 y interface\, and a shared vocabulary for design critique.\n\nWhy it reson
 ated: A reference to check designs against\, and a way to ground UX feedba
 ck in something firmer than personal taste.\n\nhttps://www.nngroup.com/art
 icles/ten-usability-heuristics/
URL:https://www.nngroup.com/articles/ten-usability-heuristics/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:684c90202ec2d0d5@resonance-log
DTSTAMP:20260905T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261214
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261215
SUMMARY:Revisit: Our PM left after 4 years. We tried running without one fo
 r 4 months.
DESCRIPTION:A startup spread its PM's work across four people for four mont
 hs. Gathering feedback and spotting broken user journeys got better by bei
 ng distributed\, since the whole team saw the problems. Prioritisation col
 lapsed: several people with good judgement produce several good lists\, no
 t one ranked one.\n\nWhy it resonated: A clear read on which parts of the 
 PM role distribute well and which do not. 'Many good lists is not one orde
 red list' is a crisp way to name the part that does not.\n\nhttps://www.re
 ddit.com/r/ProductManagement/comments/1w4e38y/our_pm_left_after_4_years_we
 _tried_running/
URL:https://www.reddit.com/r/ProductManagement/comments/1w4e38y/our_pm_left
 _after_4_years_we_tried_running/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:28bbbb26bae8735e@resonance-log
DTSTAMP:20260926T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261221
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261222
SUMMARY:Revisit: Law\, Liberty and Leviathan: AI and the Future of Human Au
 tonomy
DESCRIPTION:Laws\, markets and queues are tools for coordinating people\, a
 nd they run on individual choices: prices\, votes\, complaints. If AI can 
 coordinate without those signals\, human autonomy becomes optional\, even 
 when the AI does exactly what we ask of it. Where to keep choice depends o
 n the cost of a bad one: small for a breakfast\, very large at global scal
 e.\n\nWhy it resonated: I heard Sandberg give this talk in Oxford. The lin
 k is a recording of an earlier version. I work on AI features\, and it lef
 t me with a question to ask of each one: which decisions should stay with 
 the person using it.\n\nhttps://foresight.org/resource/law-liberty-and-lev
 iathan-ai-and-the-future-of-human-autonomy/
URL:https://foresight.org/resource/law-liberty-and-leviathan-ai-and-the-fut
 ure-of-human-autonomy/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:50cf4598604f29f3@resonance-log
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261228
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261229
SUMMARY:Revisit: Opportunity Solution Trees: Visualize Your Discovery to St
 ay Aligned and Drive Outcomes
DESCRIPTION:Stop\, pause\, question. Don't jump to the solution: validate t
 he credibility of the problem first.\n\nWhy it resonated: I wanted a solid
  method for reducing bias in how I identify problems. The tree gives me a 
 written base of customer problems that customer interviews can build on.\n
 \nhttps://www.producttalk.org/opportunity-solution-trees/
URL:https://www.producttalk.org/opportunity-solution-trees/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
